    "K0_prime": "Gleason et al. (2008), manuscript page 7 and Figure 3b: K0-prime assumed to be 4, represented intrinsically by BM2.",
    "temperature_correction": "Forensic reconstruction from the deposited rows: reducing each volume to 300 K with V_300=V_T*exp[-alpha0*(T-300 K)] and the paper's goethite alpha0=2.3e-5 K^-1, then fixing V0=66.3 A^3, gives K0=158.099 GPa. The epsilon paragraph does not print this formula, so this is recorded as a numerically recovered source protocol rather than an independently measured epsilon thermal-expansion law.",
    "volume_basis": "Depository Table 2 reports the conventional orthorhombic unit-cell volume. The source P21mn cell and this material's axis-permuted P21nm cell both contain Z=2 FeOOH."
